
#align(center)[#heading(numbering: none, outlined : false)[Abstract]]
This report retraces all the work done during a summer internship at the Cagire team.
The first part details hyperbolicity in conservation laws and the Godunov method.
The second part presents a Julia implementation of the method.
Finally the last part is a study of testcases for the Carbuncle phenomenon in the Aerosol software.
A new method develloped by the Cagire team showed better handling of these instabilities than standard finite volumes.
